# Increment (++) and Decrement (--) Operators in C#

## Description
This program demonstrates how increment (`++`) increases a variable by 1 and decrement (`--`) decreases a variable by 1.

## How It Works
- Initializes `count` to 5 and `x` to 0.
- Displays the values before increment.
- Uses `++count` to increase count by 1.
- Assigns the new value to `x`.
- Displays the updated values.
## Output
X = 6, Count = 6.
## Conclusion
This program explains how increment and decrement operators work in C#.

